-- title:
--   The unramified cyclotomic localization has maximal ideal generated by p
-- statement:
--   Let $\eta\in\mathbb C$ be a primitive $L$th root of unity, $p$ a prime with $p\nmid L$, and $\mathfrak m$ a maximal ideal of $\mathbb Z[\eta]$ containing $p$. Then the maximal ideal of $\mathbb Z[\eta]_{\mathfrak m}$ is
--   $$
--   \mathfrak m\,\mathbb Z[\eta]_{\mathfrak m}=(p).
--   $$
--
--   Consequently this localization is a discrete valuation ring with uniformizer $p$, the base for the local comparison at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/LinearAlgebra/CirculantHadamard/CyclotomicLocalBase.lean#L183-L198

